# PHP 5.6 security backports for the 2026-11-19 PHP security release (8.2.36 / 8.3.37 / 8.4.28), TG-4913.
#
# Source: Ondrej Sury's php5.6 source package 5.6.40-109+debsuryorg13.1+php+1 (packages.sury.org/php,
# debian/patches, "Backported from 8.2.36"). Each section below is one of his patches,
# hunks unchanged; only files that are not compiled into this image were left out
# (tests, NEWS, sapi/cgi, sapi/fpm, ext/zend_test). CVE numbers follow his changelog.
#
#   0390 GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg  CVE-2026-15353  SOAP information disclosure through malformed array dimensions
#   0391 GHSA-68fq-fh7h-f8gr  CVE-2026-128090 PHAR OpenSSL signature bypass via algorithm downgrade
#   0394 GHSA-qc49-hpvq-g2w6  CVE-2026-129289 request smuggling through an unread request body (main/ part only)
#   0395 GHSA-4646-p932-gw34  CVE-2026-129506 SOAP use-after-free when processing DTD entity references
#   0396 GHSA-gr4f-wgx5-jpfv  CVE-2026-129496 timezone cache use-after-free (remote code execution)
#   0397 GHSA-fm2m-fjf5-v3cp  CVE-2026-126714 partially overwritten session files (remote code execution)
#   0398 GHSA-658j-r8rw-q6mx  CVE-2026-115560 session serializer mismatch (session.upload_progress.enabled off by default)
#   0399 GHSA-f6gg-rchx-xw8j  CVE-2026-128064 mixed-case HTTPS and FTPS URLs can expose data in plaintext
#
# Not included:
#   GHSA-5j3f-64r7-f564 (CVE-2026-129538, CGI), GHSA-3mg3-cr28-46gc (CVE-2026-129292, FPM),
#   GHSA-jm4m-qfqx-967m (CVE-2026-129291, FPM): sapi/cgi and sapi/fpm are not built (Apache mod_php).
#   GHSA-mmf9-xm3v-hg2x (CVE-2026-127960): not in the php5.6 package (no header folding code in 5.6).

